  "result": "I've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-sequential-prism.md`. Nothing has been edited in the repo yet. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode in this session, so the plan needs your approval here. The code, docs and tests below all go in once you approve.\n\n**Plan summary**\n- **Type:** add `class KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])` to `src/click/types.py`, modeled on `UUIDParameterType`.\n  - Its `name` is `\"key=value\"` and its metavar is `KEY=VALUE`.\n  - It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and an empty value like `a=` is allowed.\n  - Input with no `=` or with an empty key calls `self.fail(\"{value!r} is not a valid key=value pair.\")`.\n  - A value that is already a tuple passes through unchanged.\n  - There is no singleton, since you asked for `click.KeyValue()`.\n- **Export:** add `from .types import KeyValue as KeyValue` in `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Docs and changelog:** add `KeyValue` to `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`, plus a `CHANGES.md` bullet. I'll check first whether the top version is already released.\n- **Tests:**\n  - Unit tests in `tests/test_types.py` for good and bad input.\n  - A CliRunner test in `tests/test_basic.py`, including `multiple=True`.\n  - An entry in `tests/test_info_dict.py`, if that list is meant to be exhaustive.\n- **Verification:** run the targeted tests, then the full `pytest`, and try `--set a=b` and `--set ab` by hand.",
